course: dictionary
lesson: 14652
title: Predate: come before in time
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: To predate something means to exist or happen earlier than it. The word is built from «pre», which means before, and «date», a point in time. «Dinosaurs predate humans by millions of years» means dinosaurs lived long before people did.
explain: The clue «by millions of years» tells you how far back the earlier thing is. You can say «The old church predates the school by two hundred years», so the church was there first. When you meet predate, ask yourself: which came first?
explain: Scientists use predate in a different way. When an animal predates on other animals, it hunts them and eats them. «Owls predate on mice in the dark fields» tells you owls catch and eat mice. The related word is predator, the animal that does the hunting.
fact: Predate means to exist or happen earlier than something else.
fact: Pre- means before, so the prefix in predate points to the past.
fact: Predate can also mean writing a date on a document that is earlier than the real day. This is also called backdate.
fact: In nature lessons, predate on means to hunt and eat other animals as prey.
fact: The opposite of predate in time is postdate, which means to come after.
exercise: «Dinosaurs predate humans by millions of years.» What does predate mean here? | *Come before in time | Come after in time | Shout loudly | Hunt humans
exercise: «Owls predate on mice in the dark fields.» What does predate on mean here? | Sleep near | *Hunt and eat as prey | Grow taller than | Cover with a date
exercise: Which word is the opposite of predate in time? | Backdate | Predator | *Postdate | Predict
test: «The old church predates the school by two hundred years.» Which building was built first? | They were built on the same day | Nobody knows | *The church | The school
test: «The letter was predated, so it looks older than it really is.» What did someone do to the letter? | Wrote a later date than the real day | Read it aloud | Tore the letter up | *Wrote an earlier date than the real day
exam: «The cat will predate on the mice in the barn.» In this sentence, what does predate on mean? | Come before in time | *Hunt and eat | Write a date on | Sleep in
